[i]{Minerva.name} stands off to the side of the lobby, just staring at {Silas.name} and {FoShi.name}.[/i]
[i]As you walk up to her, she turns to face you.[/i]
Minerva (Sad): "I don't even know what to say. I'm glad that he's back, but I really don't want to believe him. I had heard of some sort of monster being out there, but..."
- "At least he's safe now."
	Player (Default): "At least he's safe now."
	Minerva: "I know. I'm really glad that he's safe."
- "I know, but I'm inclined to believe him."
	Player (Sad): "I know, but I'm inclined to believe him. He seems really shaken up."
	Minerva: "Me too. I hope that he's not lying, but if he is we might be in trouble."
	Player: "Trouble? Why?"
	Minerva: "I mean what if it followed him? What then?"
	[i]She's right. If it did follow them back, you all might be in big trouble, whatever this thing is.[/i]
- "We can fight it off if it comes here."
	Player (Happy): "We can fight it off if it comes here. We have a team here, right?
	Minerva (Sad): "..."
	Minerva (Sad): "I really don't know. People I've talked to about it seemed scared of it, even if they were capable fighters."
[i]{Minerva.name} yawns.[/i]
Minerva: "It's getting late, and I'm probably not going to sleep super well tonight."
Minerva: "I'm going to go to bed now so I can sleep as much as I can. Have a good night."
[i]{Minerva.name} leaves abruptly without giving you a chance to say anything.[/i]